# Seed files are byte-exact fuzz inputs. Git classifies a file as text when its
# first bytes contain no NUL, which for a packed run of IEEE-754 doubles depends
# on the values that happen to be stored, so the classification is unstable
# across seeds. A checkout that applies end-of-line normalization to a seed
# rewrites carriage returns and line feeds inside a double and silently turns
# that seed into a different problem. Mark them binary so no filter ever runs.
*.bin binary
